@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@
+---
+name: presentation
+description: Creates or modifies a browser presentation that works as one evolving diagrammatic scene (stable entities moving through named steps), built on a reusable React scene kit. Use when the user wants a presentation, talk, or explainer made from a topic, or wants an existing presentation changed.
+---
+
+# Presentation
+
+Generate a browser presentation from a topic. A presentation is **one scene** that evolves
+through named steps: entities keep a stable id, morph when they change, enter after the
+others settle, and exit when they leave. It is not a deck of independent slides.
+"Talk" is only an informal synonym; the per-presentation entry file is `Talk.tsx`.
+
+All paths below are relative to this `SKILL.md`'s directory (`$SKILL`), never the user's
+working directory. Helper: `node $SKILL/scripts/skill-tools.mjs <command>`.
+
+## 1. Gather
+
+Ask the user **one question at a time** for anything missing; never assume what they can still tell you.
+
+1. The topic.
+2. The visual style (palette, type, mood).
+3. For each step: its content (era, title, caption) and what the diagram shows.
+
+Rules:
+- The user controls depth. If they choose to build with partial detail, proceed with what you have
+  and iterate; there is no completeness gate.
+- If the prompt already contains the topic, style, and every step, skip the questions.
+- For a key or complex step you may draw an ASCII mockup and confirm the layout. Do not do it for every step.
+
+## 2. Resolve the target and scaffold
+
+Run `node $SKILL/scripts/skill-tools.mjs detect <project dir>`. It reports `target`, `kind`,
+and which of the three contract anchors exist (detected by presence, not byte-identity):
+
+1. **build** – Vite + React + TypeScript app with a working `npm run build`.
+2. **kit** – `src/presentation-kit/` (the `Step`/`Scene` contract, stage, navigation, chrome, fit-scale canvas).
+3. **index** – `src/presentations/index.ts`, the registry mapping each presentation to its own route.
+
+Target rules (the tool applies them):
+- Empty or standalone project: scaffold at the project root.
+- Monorepo (`workspaces`, `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, or `packages/`/`apps/`): scaffold a self-contained app in `presentations/`; do not touch the monorepo root.
+- Already inside a presentation app: use it and scaffold only the missing anchors.
+
+If `needsConfirmation` is true (non-empty project missing the kit or index), **state the target
+location and wait for the user to confirm before writing anything.**
+
+Then `node $SKILL/scripts/skill-tools.mjs scaffold <project dir>` copies only the missing anchors
+(existing files are never overwritten) from `templates/bootstrap/`. Do not assume dependencies are
+installed: the tool also merges any missing dependencies and npm scripts into an existing `package.json` (never changing existing ones), so run `npm install` and `npx playwright install chromium` in the target. If the report's `wiring` field is set, the project's existing entry point is not using the router: connect it (render `<App pathname={window.location.pathname} />`) before reporting routes as reachable.
+
+The scaffold is styling-framework-neutral and ships zero presentation styling. Add Tailwind or
+another framework only if the host already uses it or the user asks.
+
+## 3. Create or modify
+
+**Create:** `node $SKILL/scripts/skill-tools.mjs new <target> <slug> "<Title>"` writes a self-contained folder
+`src/presentations/<slug>/` (`entities.ts`, `steps/*`, `Talk.tsx`) from `templates/presentation/` and registers
+it; other presentations stay untouched. Then edit it:
+- `entities.ts` – this presentation's `layoutId` namespace (ids prefixed with the slug).
+- `steps/meta.ts` – per step: `id`, `era`, `title` (one-liner), `caption` (paragraph).
+- `steps/Scene.tsx` – compose kit primitives (`Box`, `Label`, `Arrow`, `Frame`, `Emphasis`, `SymbolChip`)
+  inside `<SceneLayer>`, keyed by entity id. Steps that share a `groupKey` and Scene keep one mounted
+  scene, so add entities as the story grows rather than redrawing. Keep intentional overlaps; raw
+  `motion` elements with stable `layoutId`s are fine for coordinate-heavy diagrams.
+- Canvas is 880 × 380 design units, scaled uniformly to fit.
+- **Styling lives in the presentation** (a `style.css` imported by `Talk.tsx`, plain CSS by default),
+  never in `src/presentation-kit/`, which has no styling defaults. Style the hooks: `data-presentation-*`
+  attributes, entity kinds, the active dot / ToC entry (`[data-presentation-active='true']`, `aria-current`),
+  and `[data-presentation-attribution]` so the "made by and-scene" link is legible. Do not add a top-left brand unless asked.
+
+**Modify:** if the target is missing or ambiguous, list the registered presentations and ask which one
+before changing anything. Then ask only about the requested changes (steps, entities, or style) and edit
+that presentation in place; do not re-run the create flow.
+
+## 4. Self-verify before reporting done
+
+Never report success while a check fails. Fix, then re-run.
+
+1. `npm run build` – no type errors.
+2. Render check – at least the first step renders with no console/runtime errors; `npm run verify` renders every step.
+3. Visual composition – `npm run inspect -- <slug>` (project-local helper; prefer it over ad hoc scripts, and put any
+   temporary Playwright script under the project root so dependencies resolve locally). It writes settled per-step
+   screenshots to `.inspection/<slug>/<viewport>/` and prints advisory warnings. Look at the first step, the last step,
+   and dense/key steps; for responsive-sensitive presentations also run `-- --viewport 390x844`.
+4. Review every warning: fix accidental text/chrome collisions, indistinct current-step chrome, and unpolished
+   attribution in the presentation's CSS. Mark a genuinely intentional, readable overlap only by adding
+   `data-presentation-allow-overlap` (kit export `ALLOW_OVERLAP`, via the primitive's `dataAttrs`) on that subtree.
+
+Report the final build/verify results and any remaining advisory warnings accurately.
diff --git a/skills/presentation/scripts/skill-tools.mjs b/skills/presentation/scripts/skill-tools.mjs
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..604f63e6f64ecdc4e7fed796680b95a68ebf49f7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/skills/presentation/scripts/skill-tools.mjs
@@ -0,0 +1,286 @@
+// Helpers behind skills/presentation/SKILL.md: detect scaffold anchors and the target,
+// scaffold missing anchors, create + register a presentation. Templates are resolved
+// relative to this file, never the caller's working directory.
+//
+//   skill-tools.mjs detect [dir]
+//   skill-tools.mjs scaffold [dir] [--anchors build,kit,index]
+//   skill-tools.mjs new <dir> <slug> <title>
+//   skill-tools.mjs register <dir> <slug> <title>
+import { cpSync, existsSync, mkdirSync, readFileSync, readdirSync, statSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs'
+import path from 'node:path'
+import { fileURLToPath, pathToFileURL } from 'node:url'
+
+export const TEMPLATES = fileURLToPath(new URL('../templates/', import.meta.url))
+const BOOTSTRAP = path.join(TEMPLATES, 'bootstrap')
+const PRESENTATION = path.join(TEMPLATES, 'presentation')
+export const ANCHORS = ['build', 'kit', 'index']
+
+/** Files (relative to an app root) each anchor owns. */
+const ANCHOR_FILES = {
+  build: [
+    'package.json',
+    'package-lock.json',
+    'index.html',
+    'vite.config.ts',
+    'tsconfig.json',
+    'tsconfig.app.json',
+    'tsconfig.node.json',
+    'eslint.config.js',
+    '.gitignore',
+    'public',
+    'src/main.tsx',
+    'src/index.css',
+  ],
+  kit: ['src/presentation-kit'],
+  index: ['src/presentations', 'src/Landing.tsx', 'src/router.ts', 'src/App.tsx'],
+}
+
+/** Verification/inspection scripts every presentation app needs, whichever anchors are being scaffolded. */
+const TOOLING_FILES = ['scripts']
+
+const SOURCE_EXTS = ['ts', 'tsx', 'js', 'jsx', 'mjs']
+const findFile = (root, dir, base) =>
+  readdirSync(path.join(root, dir)).find((n) => SOURCE_EXTS.some((e) => n === `${base}.${e}`))
+
+const SLUG = /^[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*$/
+
+const readJson = (file) => {
+  try {
+    return JSON.parse(readFileSync(file, 'utf8'))
+  } catch {
+    return null
+  }
+}
+
+function hasBuildSetup(root) {
+  const pkg = readJson(path.join(root, 'package.json'))
+  if (!pkg?.scripts?.build) return false
+  const deps = { ...pkg.dependencies, ...pkg.devDependencies }
+  const viteConfig = ['ts', 'js', 'mjs', 'mts'].some((ext) => existsSync(path.join(root, `vite.config.${ext}`)))
+  return viteConfig && ['react', 'react-dom', 'vite', 'typescript'].every((d) => d in deps)
+}
+
+/** Contract-level anchor detection: presence of the pieces, not byte-identical files. */
+export function anchorsAt(root) {
+  return {
+    build: hasBuildSetup(root),
+    kit: existsSync(path.join(root, 'src/presentation-kit')) && ['Presentation', 'types'].every((b) => findFile(root, 'src/presentation-kit', b)),
+    index: existsSync(path.join(root, 'src/presentations')) && Boolean(findFile(root, 'src/presentations', 'index')),
+  }
+}
+
+function isEmptyDir(dir) {
+  return !existsSync(dir) || readdirSync(dir).filter((n) => n !== '.git').length === 0
+}
+
+export function isMonorepo(dir) {
+  const pkg = readJson(path.join(dir, 'package.json'))
+  if (pkg?.workspaces) return true
+  if (existsSync(path.join(dir, 'pnpm-workspace.yaml'))) return true
+  return ['packages', 'apps'].some((d) => existsSync(path.join(dir, d)) && statSync(path.join(dir, d)).isDirectory())
+}
+
+/**
+ * Resolve where the presentation app lives and which anchors it lacks.
+ * kind: 'existing-app' | 'empty' | 'monorepo' | 'standalone'
+ */
+export function detect(dir) {
+  dir = path.resolve(dir)
+  const candidates = [dir, path.join(dir, 'presentations')]
+  const appRoot = candidates.find((c) => {
+    const a = anchorsAt(c)
+    return a.kit || a.index
+  })
+  let target = dir
+  let kind
+  if (appRoot) {
+    target = appRoot
+    kind = 'existing-app'
+  } else if (isEmptyDir(dir)) {
+    kind = 'empty'
+  } else if (isMonorepo(dir)) {
+    target = path.join(dir, 'presentations')
+    kind = 'monorepo'
+  } else {
+    kind = 'standalone'
+  }
+  const anchors = anchorsAt(target)
+  const missing = ANCHORS.filter((a) => !anchors[a])
+  const sceneMissing = !anchors.kit || !anchors.index
+  return {
+    dir,
+    target,
+    kind,
+    anchors,
+    missing,
+    needsConfirmation: kind !== 'empty' && sceneMissing,
+  }
+}
+
+function copyMissing(from, to, report) {
+  if (!existsSync(from)) return
+  if (statSync(from).isDirectory()) {
+    for (const name of readdirSync(from)) copyMissing(path.join(from, name), path.join(to, name), report)
+    return
+  }
+  if (existsSync(to)) {
+    report.skipped.push(to)
+    return
+  }
+  mkdirSync(path.dirname(to), { recursive: true })
+  cpSync(from, to)
+  report.created.push(to)
+}
+
+/** Add dependencies/scripts that are absent from an existing package.json; never change existing ones. */
+function mergePackageJson(target, report) {
+  const file = path.join(target, 'package.json')
+  const have = readJson(file)
+  const want = readJson(path.join(BOOTSTRAP, 'package.json'))
+  if (!have) return
+  let changed = false
+  for (const section of ['dependencies', 'devDependencies', 'scripts']) {
+    for (const [name, value] of Object.entries(want[section] ?? {})) {
+      // A dependency already present in the other section counts as present.
+      const present = section === 'scripts' ? name in (have.scripts ?? {}) : name in { ...have.dependencies, ...have.devDependencies }
+      if (present) continue
+      have[section] = { ...have[section], [name]: value }
+      report.added.push(`${section}.${name}`)
+      changed = true
+    }
+  }
+  if (changed) writeFileSync(file, JSON.stringify(have, null, 2) + '\n')
+}
+
+/** Copy the files of the given anchors from templates/bootstrap, never overwriting existing files. */
+export function scaffold(target, anchors = ANCHORS) {
+  target = path.resolve(target)
+  const report = { target, created: [], skipped: [], added: [], wiring: null }
+  for (const anchor of anchors) if (!ANCHORS.includes(anchor)) throw new Error(`unknown anchor "${anchor}"`)
+  mkdirSync(target, { recursive: true })
+  const hadPackage = existsSync(path.join(target, 'package.json'))
+  const files = [...anchors.flatMap((a) => ANCHOR_FILES[a]), ...TOOLING_FILES]
+  for (const rel of files) {
+    if (rel === 'package-lock.json' && hadPackage) continue
+    copyMissing(path.join(BOOTSTRAP, rel), path.join(target, rel), report)
+  }
+  // Kit, index and tooling all need the template's dependencies and npm scripts, even when the
+  // build setup itself already exists.
+  if (hadPackage) mergePackageJson(target, report)
+  if (anchors.includes('index')) {
+    const main = path.join(target, 'src/main.tsx')
+    if (!existsSync(main) || !/\bpathname\b/.test(readFileSync(main, 'utf8'))) {
+      report.wiring = 'The project entry point does not use the router: render <App pathname={window.location.pathname} /> from src/App.tsx (or call resolveRoute from src/router.ts) so each presentation is reachable at /<slug>. An existing src/main.tsx is never overwritten.'
+    }
+  }
+  report.created = report.created.map((f) => path.relative(target, f))
+  report.skipped = report.skipped.map((f) => path.relative(target, f))
+  return report
+}
+
+/** Index of the `]` closing the array literal that opens at `open`, skipping strings and comments. */
+function matchingBracket(source, open) {
+  let depth = 0
+  for (let i = open; i < source.length; i++) {
+    const c = source[i]
+    if (c === "'" || c === '"' || c === '`') {
+      for (i++; i < source.length && source[i] !== c; i++) if (source[i] === '\\') i++
+    } else if (c === '/' && source[i + 1] === '/') {
+      i = source.indexOf('\n', i)
+      if (i < 0) break
+    } else if (c === '/' && source[i + 1] === '*') {
+      i = source.indexOf('*/', i + 2) + 1
+    } else if (c === '[' || c === '(' || c === '{') depth++
+    else if (c === ']' || c === ')' || c === '}') {
+      depth--
+      if (depth === 0) return i
+    }
+  }
+  return -1
+}
+
+/** Insert a registry entry into the `presentations` array; existing entries are left untouched. */
+export function register(target, slug, title) {
+  if (!SLUG.test(slug)) throw new Error(`invalid slug "${slug}": use lowercase words joined by hyphens`)
+  const dir = path.join(target, 'src/presentations')
+  const name = existsSync(dir) && findFile(target, 'src/presentations', 'index')
+  if (!name) throw new Error('presentation index not found; scaffold the index anchor first')
+  const file = path.join(dir, name)
+  const source = readFileSync(file, 'utf8')
+  if (new RegExp(`slug:\\s*['"]${slug}['"]`).test(source)) throw new Error(`"${slug}" is already registered`)
+  const declaration = /\bpresentations\b[^=\n]*=\s*\[/.exec(source)
+  if (!declaration) throw new Error('could not find the `presentations` array in the registry')
+  const open = declaration.index + declaration[0].length - 1
+  const close = matchingBracket(source, open)
+  if (close < 0) throw new Error('could not find the end of the registry array')
+  const entry = `  {\n    slug: '${slug}',\n    title: ${JSON.stringify(title)},\n    load: () => import('./${slug}/Talk.tsx'),\n  },\n`
+  let before = source.slice(0, close).replace(/\s*$/, '')
+  if (!before.endsWith(',') && !before.endsWith('[')) before += ','
+  writeFileSync(file, `${before}\n${entry}${source.slice(close)}`)
+  return file
+}
+
+function materialize(from, to, tokens) {
+  mkdirSync(to, { recursive: true })
+  for (const name of readdirSync(from)) {
+    const src = path.join(from, name)
+    if (statSync(src).isDirectory()) {
+      materialize(src, path.join(to, name), tokens)
+      continue
+    }
+    let text = readFileSync(src, 'utf8')
+    for (const [token, value] of Object.entries(tokens)) text = text.replaceAll(token, () => value)
+    writeFileSync(path.join(to, name), text)
+  }
+}
+
+/** Write templates/presentation into src/presentations/<slug>/ (no registration). */
+export function createPresentationFiles(target, slug, title) {
+  if (!SLUG.test(slug)) throw new Error(`invalid slug "${slug}": use lowercase words joined by hyphens`)
+  const dest = path.join(target, 'src/presentations', slug)
+  if (existsSync(dest)) throw new Error(`${path.relative(target, dest)} already exists`)
+  materialize(PRESENTATION, dest, { __SLUG__: slug, __TITLE__: JSON.stringify(title) })
+  return dest
+}
+
+/** Create a self-contained presentation folder and register it. */
+export function newPresentation(target, slug, title) {
+  const dest = createPresentationFiles(target, slug, title)
+  register(target, slug, title)
+  return dest
+}
+
+function main(argv) {
+  const [cmd, ...rest] = argv
+  const flag = (name) => {
+    const at = rest.indexOf(`--${name}`)
+    return at >= 0 ? rest[at + 1] : undefined
+  }
+  const pos = rest.filter((a, i) => !a.startsWith('--') && !(i > 0 && rest[i - 1].startsWith('--')))
+  switch (cmd) {
+    case 'detect':
+      return console.log(JSON.stringify(detect(pos[0] ?? '.'), null, 2))
+    case 'scaffold': {
+      const dir = pos[0] ?? '.'
+      const info = detect(dir)
+      const anchors = flag('anchors') ? flag('anchors').split(',') : info.missing
+      return console.log(JSON.stringify(scaffold(info.target, anchors), null, 2))
+    }
+    case 'new':
+      return console.log(newPresentation(path.resolve(pos[0]), pos[1], pos[2]))
+    case 'register':
+      return console.log(register(path.resolve(pos[0]), pos[1], pos[2]))
+    default:
+      console.error('usage: skill-tools.mjs detect|scaffold|new|register ...')
+      process.exitCode = 2
+  }
+}
+
+if (process.argv[1] && import.meta.url === pathToFileURL(process.argv[1]).href) {
+  try {
+    main(process.argv.slice(2))
+  } catch (e) {
+    console.error(e.message)
+    process.exitCode = 1
+  }
+}
